{"journal_version":1,"sequence":11,"replace_from":17,"message_count":18,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"Done. Report concisely.","content":"## Change\n\n**`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`**\n- Added an `attempt` counter alongside the existing `state`. The polling effect is now keyed on `attempt`: it still uses the same 120 ms simulated delay and reads `?sync=error` only on the initial attempt, so the first load behaves exactly as before (error at `/?sync=error`, success at `/`), while a retry always resolves to success.\n- `retry()` sets the state back to `'loading'` (rendering `Checking service…`) and increments `attempt`; the effect's existing `clearTimeout` cleanup guarantees at most one live timer, so repeated activation cannot overlap timers, and unmount still clears it.\n- Rendered `Retry sync` as a `type=\"button\"` inside the existing error block, so it exists only in the error state, disappears on success, does no navigation/reload, and — since `AsyncPanel` keeps its own local state — cannot reset the selected task in `App`.\n\n**`src/styles.css`**\n- Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; margin-top: 8px; }` so the new button keeps the shared `button` styling but isn't stretched full-width by the error block's grid layout.\n\n## Commands run\n\n- `npm run verify:agent` — which runs `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`) and `npm run test:public` (`playwright test`). Both green: build succeeded, 6/6 public tests passed.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- Retry behavior itself is covered only by manual reasoning; the public suite has no error/retry test, and I did not add tests (task forbade modifying existing ones, and none were requested).\n- A retry always succeeds by design; there is no path back to the error state after the first attempt. If a hidden test expects the query param to be re-read on retry, that would fail — but the acceptance criteria state retry completes as synced, so this matches the spec.\n- The retry button inherits the `button:focus-visible` outline and is inside the existing `role=\"alert\"` region; `aria-live=\"polite\"` behavior on the parent is unchanged.","response_items":[{"id":"f4798623-0ed4-41ba-8796-538aa765df0c","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"Done. Report concisely.","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":"a1cbe87b-d10e-4980-a6a8-54b839738089-0","status":"completed"},{"id":"b740c8b3-2731-4300-a1db-f9e0e5138c36","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"## Change\n\n**`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`**\n- Added an `attempt` counter alongside the existing `state`. The polling effect is now keyed on `attempt`: it still uses the same 120 ms simulated delay and reads `?sync=error` only on the initial attempt, so the first load behaves exactly as before (error at `/?sync=error`, success at `/`), while a retry always resolves to success.\n- `retry()` sets the state back to `'loading'` (rendering `Checking service…`) and increments `attempt`; the effect's existing `clearTimeout` cleanup guarantees at most one live timer, so repeated activation cannot overlap timers, and unmount still clears it.\n- Rendered `Retry sync` as a `type=\"button\"` inside the existing error block, so it exists only in the error state, disappears on success, does no navigation/reload, and — since `AsyncPanel` keeps its own local state — cannot reset the selected task in `App`.\n\n**`src/styles.css`**\n- Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; margin-top: 8px; }` so the new button keeps the shared `button` styling but isn't stretched full-width by the error block's grid layout.\n\n## Commands run\n\n- `npm run verify:agent` — which runs `npm run build` (`tsc --noEmit && vite build`) and `npm run test:public` (`playwright test`). Both green: build succeeded, 6/6 public tests passed.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- Retry behavior itself is covered only by manual reasoning; the public suite has no error/retry test, and I did not add tests (task forbade modifying existing ones, and none were requested).\n- A retry always succeeds by design; there is no path back to the error state after the first attempt. If a hidden test expects the query param to be re-read on retry, that would fail — but the acceptance criteria state retry completes as synced, so this matches the spec.\n- The retry button inherits the `button:focus-visible` outline and is inside the existing `role=\"alert\"` region; `aria-live=\"polite\"` behavior on the parent is unchanged.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T15:56:48.643253+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":35932,"context_tokens":7124,"step_count":7,"markup_recovered":0,"recent_call_hashes":["41a19181bbd813f18f2f604051ce7cea","54c6d4923513570e71525b862782cc14","0b2507d4e6e12b98774fdb7da83e9c8c","22c5ff12f36f01d15d042e587aa72016","95feef7d3cfa57ab50d4ac49f8ef55ca","af7899898ccdaf79dc3cefb51afadb04","8f0d9b45b1d9f0950e534f7c51a3dbca","41a19181bbd813f18f2f604051ce7cea","3c45d71dcb1acaddc13d0e86e5418077"],"reads_since_last_edit":1,"has_landed_write":true,"low_yield_since_progress":0,"distinct_evidence_count":8,"scout_ledger":[{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx (30 lines total, showing 1-30) 1 import { useEffect, useState } from 'react'; 2 3 type State = 'loading' | 'success' | 'error'; 4 5 export function AsyncPanel() { 6 const [state, setState] = useState<Stat"},{"tool":"file_read","target":"TASK.md","outcome":"hit","snippet":"File: TASK.md (16 lines total, showing 1-16) 1 # T03 — Recoverable asynchronous error state 2 3 Add a recovery action to the remote-sync error state. 4 5 Acceptance criteria: 6 7 - The existing success path at `/` remains unchanged and neve"},{"tool":"file_read","target":"src/styles.css","outcome":"hit","snippet":"Fil